    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d631">

                <pb facs="0607" n="1341" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1341"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr. Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Barnum telegraphs American property destroyed in Harpoot $100,000 probably. I
                    have notified the Porte would expect prompt payment for <pb facs="0608" n="1342"
                        xml:id="pg1342"/> all damages when extent is known. Telegram states that
                    shell burst in missionary house; that soldiers protected raiders and joined in
                    plunder, and that multitudes were killed in that province. Persons of
                    missionaries there protected.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
